# Saegim Flutter Project Rules

## Project Context
- **Project**: Saegim Mobile App
- **Framework**: Flutter 3.35.3 with Dart 3.9.2  
- **Platforms**: Android & iOS
- **Architecture**: Clean Architecture (recommended)

## Code Style Guidelines
- Use **2 spaces** for indentation (Dart, YAML, JSON)
- **Line length**: 80 characters max
- **File naming**: snake_case for Dart files
- **Class naming**: PascalCase
- **Variable naming**: camelCase
- **Constants**: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE

## Flutter Best Practices
- Always use `const` constructors when possible
- Prefer composition over inheritance
- Use meaningful widget names
- Implement proper error handling
- Follow Material Design guidelines
- Use proper state management (Provider/Riverpod/Bloc)

## File Organization
```
lib/
├── main.dart
├── app/
├── core/
├── features/
│   ├── feature_name/
│   │   ├── data/
│   │   ├── domain/
│   │   └── presentation/
└── shared/
```

## Development Preferences
- **Language**: Korean for comments and documentation
- **Testing**: Write tests for business logic
- **Performance**: Consider widget rebuilds
- **Accessibility**: Implement proper semantics